{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/ben/github/toulmin/evals/toulmin/variants/ask-only/skills/toulmin\n\n# Writing the piece\n\nBefore you write, ask the user for what you are missing. Send one message with at most five questions, the most useful first. Ask only what would change the piece and what the request does not already answer. When the answers come back, write the piece as you normally would, and hand it over. When the user does not know something, write without it and do not guess.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: One-page written case for promotion from assistant front office manager to front office manager at a 180-room hotel, addressed to the general manager, due Friday. User wants it to claim they're the main reason guest check-in scores rose (7.9 to 8.6 over 18 months), but a full lobby/room renovation happened at the same time. Other facts: 6 years tenure, 2 as AFOM; rewrote training (solo after 5 shifts vs 9); turnover 9/14 the year before AFOM, 5/14 last year; covered FOM role alone 7 weeks; never managed a budget, FOM owns $1.1M payroll budget."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb90b47d-0f34-41ef-817b-bd5e59de9d3c","uuid":"2dc08f91-f14e-4586-a56d-e35c048f5aca","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:22:47.709Z","isSynthetic":true}
